The method follows MRI2vid.py (https://github.com/thomshaw92/MRI2Vid), kept in
apps/mri2vid.

src/vendor/mp4-muxer.js and src/vendor/webm-muxer.js are esbuild bundles of
mp4-muxer 5.2.2 and webm-muxer 5.1.4 by Vanilagy, MIT licence
(https://github.com/Vanilagy/mp4-muxer, https://github.com/Vanilagy/webm-muxer).

src/font8x8.js is font8x8_basic by Daniel Hepper, public domain
(https://github.com/dhepper/font8x8, commit 8e279d2d864e79128e96188a6b9526cfa3fbfef9).

The command line depends on @libav.js/variant-vp9-opus 6.10.9, installed
unmodified as its own module under node_modules/. It is libav.js 6.10.9.0
(https://github.com/Yahweasel/libav.js, tag v6.10.9.0, commit
c80e885c3461f7bb7ea565c9631b34243ae0dbf1) compiled with Emscripten from
FFmpeg 9.0 (LGPL-2.1-or-later), libvpx 1.16.0 (BSD-3-Clause) and Opus 1.6.1
(BSD-3-Clause). The full licence texts are at the top of each
dist/libav-6.10.9.0-vp9-opus.*.mjs and .js file in that module. The
corresponding source and build scripts are the libav.js tag above, which
fetches the FFmpeg, libvpx and Opus release archives it names. You may
replace the module with your own build of the same interface.
